        "paragraphs": [
            "IBM Granite is a family of AI models developed by IBM. IBM says the models are open source under an Apache 2.0 license, cryptographically signed and ISO certified, and are designed for scalable, enterprise workloads. IBM says Granite 4.0 introduces a hybrid Mamba-2/transformer architecture, with a Mixture-of-Experts strategy in select models, and that Granite 4.0 Small achieves industry-leading results in key agentic tasks like instruction following and function calling.",
            "The family is organised into several lines. Granite Language includes Granite 4.2, Granite 4.1 and Granite 4.0, with sizes such as Granite 4.2 3B, Granite 4.2 8B, Granite 4.2 30B, Granite 4.1 3B, Granite 4.1 8B, Granite-4.0-H-Small, Granite-4.0-H-Tiny, Granite-4.0-H-Micro, Granite-4.0-Micro, Granite-4.0-H-1B, Granite-4.0-1B, Granite-4.0-H-350M and Granite-4.0-350M. Related lines include Granite Speech, Granite Vision, Granite Guardian, Granite Embedding, Granite Time Series and Granite Docling. Granite-Speech-5.0-470M-TurboCTC is a speech model with 470M parameters.",
            "IBM offers the models for download and through Hugging Face, GitHub, Ollama, vLLM (Containerized), LM Studio, watsonx.ai, OpenRouter, Replicate, Weights & Biases, Unsloth and AnythingLLM. IBM also provides a Granite model selector to find models that fit available resources and offer the required capabilities."
        ],
